      "title": "👑 Pixaroma - Note - START HERE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MODELS AND NODES USED IN THIS WORKFLOW  \n\n---\n\n### Models are downloaded automatically the first time you use the workflow.\n \n---\n\n## 🧩 Nodes Installed from Manager  \n\n- ComfyUI-Easy-Use\n- Qwen3-TTS - Voice Synthesis & Cloning\n- ComfyUI_LayerStyle\n\nRead More about Qwen TTS Node [HERE](https://github.com/flybirdxx/ComfyUI-Qwen-TTS)\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources  \n🎥 **Tutorials:** [Pixaroma YouTube Channel](https://www.youtube.com/@pixaroma)  \n💬 **Community Discord:** [Join Here](https://discord.com/invite/gggpkVgBf3)\n\n---\n\n## 🎭 Qwen3 Dialogue Workflow (Using Previously Saved Voices)\n\nGenerate a multi-speaker dialogue using voices you already saved with **SaveVoice**.\n\n### 🧠 What It Does\n- Loads 2 saved voices (example: `my_custom_voice.wav` + `my_custom_voice2.wav`)\n- Assigns them to roles in **RoleBank** (role_name_1 = man, role_name_2 = woman)\n- Generates a full dialogue using **DialogueInference**\n- Outputs a single MP3 (merged dialogue)\n\n### ✍️ How To Use\n1. **Load Previous Saved Voice (man)**  \n   - Pick your saved voice file (Press **R** to refresh the list)\n\n2. **Load Previous Saved Voice (woman)**  \n   - Pick your second saved voice file (Press **R** to refresh)\n\n3. **Dialogue**  \n   - Write your script in this format (one line per speaker):  \n     `man: dialogue text`  \n     `woman: dialogue text`\n\n4. **RoleBank**\n   - Make sure `role_name_1 = man` and `role_name_2 = woman` match your dialogue labels\n\n5. Click **Run**\n\n### 💾 MP3 Save Location\n- Preview inside **Save Audio (MP3)**\n- Saves under: `ComfyUI\\output\\audio"
      ],
